  "id": "ne",
  "term": "NE",
  "definition": "NE, also called error negativity or error-related negativity, is a brain-wave signal seen in EEG as a brief negative shift about 50 milliseconds after a person makes an error. It is understood as reflecting the brain’s processing of errors and has been studied in relation to later behavioral adjustment.",
